{
  "task": {
    "id": "Prob045_edgedetect2",
    "spec": "\r\nI would like you to implement a module named TopModule with the following\r\ninterface. All input and output ports are one bit unless otherwise\r\nspecified.\r\n\r\n - input clk\r\n - input in       (8 bits)\r\n - output anyedge (8 bits)\r\n\r\nImplement a module that for each bit in an 8-bit input vector, detect\r\nwhen the input signal changes from one clock cycle to the next (detect\r\nany edge). The output bit of anyedge should be set to 1 the cycle \r\nafter the input bit has 0 to 1 or 1 to 0 transition occurs. Assume all \r\nsequential logic is triggered on the positive edge of the clock.\r\n\r\n",
    "interface": {
      "top": "TopModule",
      "ports": [
        {
          "name": "clk",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 1,
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "in",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 8,
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "anyedge",
          "direction": "output",
          "width": 8,
          "signed": false
        }
      ]
    },
    "constraints": "SystemVerilog, single self-contained TopModule DUT; xczu3eg-sbva484-1-e; 5 ns synthesis clock; simulator seed 1. No reference dependencies, hierarchy outside the DUT, file access, includes or DPI."
  },
  "sample_id": "83e1136b-1eb3-4fb4-a3e6-22332e5f01cc",
  "variant_id": "C",
  "current": {
    "revision_id": "972059fa-e329-47a3-b209-4841fa172ab6",
    "source_sha256": "1def3b762711b914476fd71991a715f5aaee8649d7b104b8c75bdb633a6f3ada",
    "source": "\nmodule TopModule (\n    input  logic       clk,\n    input  logic [7:0] in,\n    output logic [7:0] anyedge\n);\n\n    logic [7:0] prev;\n\n    always_ff @(posedge clk) begin\n        prev <= in;\n    end\n\n    assign anyedge = in ^ prev;\n\nendmodule\n"
  },
